1
00:00:10,410 --> 00:00:14,467
[Subtitles by danielsangeo]

2
00:00:17,538 --> 00:00:21,578
--where I'm supposed to be
going... whoa... wait.

3
00:00:21,578 --> 00:00:23,000
Something happened.

4
00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:26,691
Okay, I guess I came in
through this door...?

5
00:00:26,691 --> 00:00:28,133
Why did I lock this?

6
00:00:29,957 --> 00:00:32,106
Shit...

7
00:00:32,106 --> 00:00:33,922
Did I black out again?

8
00:00:33,922 --> 00:00:35,570
Why am I standing?

9
00:00:35,570 --> 00:00:37,993
Memory...

10
00:00:37,993 --> 00:00:39,630
So, what do I remember?

11
00:00:39,630 --> 00:00:39,855
I remember--

12
00:00:39,855 --> 00:00:41,513
[explosion]
Waah!

13
00:00:41,513 --> 00:00:43,879
I remember gas filling the room,

14
00:00:43,879 --> 00:00:46,457
[missile whistling]
ghost... wizards...

15
00:00:46,457 --> 00:00:48,597
[explosion]
Ooooooh!

16
00:00:48,597 --> 00:00:51,192
Oh, wow!

17
00:00:51,192 --> 00:00:54,737
That... that would've hurt.

18
00:00:54,737 --> 00:00:55,477
Uh oh.

19
00:00:55,477 --> 00:00:56,320
GUARD: Open up the reactor--

20
00:00:56,320 --> 00:00:57,864
Hold it right there!

21
00:00:57,864 --> 00:00:58,669
GUARD: --to safety.

22
00:00:58,669 --> 00:01:02,309
SCIENTIST: I'm sorry but those doors will
not open until we send the All Clear.

23
00:01:02,309 --> 00:01:04,443
A ventriloquist!
GUARD: Then send it already!

24
00:01:04,443 --> 00:01:05,827
SCIENTIST: I would love to do that,

25
00:01:05,827 --> 00:01:09,379
SCIENTIST: but the aerial bombardment
has made a wreck of my transmitter.

26
00:01:09,379 --> 00:01:12,340
SCIENTIST: The cables are severed;
we'd have to aim it by hand,

27
00:01:12,340 --> 00:01:15,351
SCIENTIST: and I'm getting high
radiation levels in the transmitter dome.

28
00:01:15,351 --> 00:01:16,789
SCIENTIST: Nobody but a
fool would go in there.

29
00:01:16,789 --> 00:01:18,901
I pity the fool!
GUARD: What about this guy?

30
00:01:19,791 --> 00:01:22,925
SCIENTIST: Yes. You could
survive in that suit of yours.

31
00:01:22,925 --> 00:01:26,338
SCIENTIST: Very well. I will lower
security on the satellite access elevator

32
00:01:26,338 --> 00:01:27,734
SCIENTIST: and you can go up
into the dome.

33
00:01:27,734 --> 00:01:29,700
No...
SCIENTIST: I'll try to help you over the intercom.

34
00:01:29,700 --> 00:01:31,909
Whoa-whoa. Who are you?

35
00:01:31,909 --> 00:01:35,082
I'm Gordon! I can do both your jobs.

36
00:01:35,082 --> 00:01:38,732
You people talk like you know
what you're doing, but you don't.

37
00:01:38,732 --> 00:01:40,701
Oh, "Loading Bay", that's good!

38
00:01:41,706 --> 00:01:44,131
What? What are you aiming at?

39
00:01:44,131 --> 00:01:47,011
Man, you two are higher than I am!

40
00:01:47,011 --> 00:01:49,525
You're all just fronting. I've
seen too much of that.

41
00:01:49,525 --> 00:01:51,098
GUARD: I'll stay here and guard this area.

42
00:01:51,098 --> 00:01:55,406
Yeah, keep us safe from the
empty elevator, Scooby. I'm leaving.

43
00:01:55,406 --> 00:01:58,296
That guy said they're
going down to safety.

44
00:01:58,296 --> 00:02:00,371
Going down isn't safe.

45
00:02:00,371 --> 00:02:02,418
Going UP isn't safe.

46
00:02:02,418 --> 00:02:05,188
Those two are probably dead by now.

47
00:02:05,188 --> 00:02:08,166
Getting away from here could be MORE safe.

48
00:02:08,166 --> 00:02:11,348
I think the President has
pretty good security.

49
00:02:11,348 --> 00:02:15,819
Hey, maybe I could disguise myself--
no, wait, that wouldn't work.

50
00:02:15,819 --> 00:02:18,282
I would need a professional
makeup artist.

51
00:02:18,282 --> 00:02:21,119
Eddie can't do makeup for shit.

52
00:02:21,119 --> 00:02:24,700
Well, I would've preferred
another snack machine, but, y'know,

53
00:02:24,700 --> 00:02:26,873
sugar's the same as food, right?

54
00:02:26,873 --> 00:02:29,156
Hey, wait! I don't have to pay for this!

55
00:02:29,156 --> 00:02:32,834
In Black Mesa, I am king
of the vending machines.

56
00:02:33,591 --> 00:02:34,569
Yeah!

57
00:02:34,569 --> 00:02:35,260
Yeah ha ha!

58
00:02:35,260 --> 00:02:36,156
Oh... Ow!

59
00:02:36,156 --> 00:02:36,847
Shit...

60
00:02:37,644 --> 00:02:38,540
Okay...

61
00:02:38,540 --> 00:02:39,367
[explosion]
Whoa...

62
00:02:40,712 --> 00:02:41,686
[explosion]
JESUS!

63
00:02:41,686 --> 00:02:44,540
This is bad soda! I'm not
drinking that!

64
00:02:44,540 --> 00:02:48,901
Let me out of here, Captain...
Woody of the... Box... Brigade...

65
00:02:49,892 --> 00:02:51,834
I've seen you before.

66
00:02:52,856 --> 00:02:57,012
I can't decide if I'd rather
have food or more bullets.

67
00:02:57,012 --> 00:02:59,550
I'm not eating this thing;
I know that much.

68
00:02:59,550 --> 00:03:00,033
Hey!

69
00:03:02,866 --> 00:03:06,450
This is an illegal gathering of
three or more freaks.

70
00:03:06,450 --> 00:03:09,426
GUARD: Ooh, I bet you're glad I've
got this old sidearm on me, aren't ya?

71
00:03:09,426 --> 00:03:11,884
You didn't fired a single shot.

72
00:03:11,884 --> 00:03:14,481
Are you being serious, sir?

73
00:03:14,481 --> 00:03:16,058
Yeah, my hero.

74
00:03:16,058 --> 00:03:18,234
Bet you don't have one of these, huh?

75
00:03:18,704 --> 00:03:19,767
Does this bug you?

76
00:03:20,548 --> 00:03:22,969
You didn't even blink. Jesus...

77
00:03:22,969 --> 00:03:24,166
What are you?

78
00:03:24,166 --> 00:03:27,418
Never mind, just don't make
me kill us both, okay?

79
00:03:27,418 --> 00:03:28,901
I hate when that happens.

80
00:03:29,908 --> 00:03:32,554
Oh, here we go. Some magazines.

81
00:03:32,554 --> 00:03:36,133
This will buy me at least
five more minutes of life.

82
00:03:36,802 --> 00:03:40,845
I wonder if insurance rates for
Black Mesa survivors go up.

83
00:03:40,845 --> 00:03:44,269
Like, adjustors would say if
you're in one alien invasion,

84
00:03:44,269 --> 00:03:46,821
that means you're at risk for another.

85
00:03:46,821 --> 00:03:50,334
Ah, who am I kidding? There's
not going to be any survivors.

86
00:03:51,481 --> 00:03:55,248
Like, even with the military,
I don't see that happening.

87
00:03:55,248 --> 00:03:56,895
Oh, wow, you're no fun.

88
00:03:56,895 --> 00:03:59,451
I'll show you the... meaning of... fun...

89
00:03:59,451 --> 00:04:00,868
[explosion]

90
00:04:02,696 --> 00:04:03,829
Yeah.

91
00:04:03,829 --> 00:04:06,498
Are we having fun yet?

92
00:04:06,498 --> 00:04:07,874
Sure looks like it.

93
00:04:07,874 --> 00:04:11,375
Huh, the Laser Tag Extreme Fun Zone.

94
00:04:11,375 --> 00:04:13,520
Oh, you think I don't see you?

95
00:04:13,520 --> 00:04:15,705
That will enhance the fun.

96
00:04:15,705 --> 00:04:18,078
Well, everybody likes surprises.

97
00:04:18,078 --> 00:04:20,149
Quick, painless surprises.

98
00:04:20,149 --> 00:04:21,310
[explosion]

99
00:04:21,310 --> 00:04:22,634
Surprise!

100
00:04:23,755 --> 00:04:24,386
What the--?

101
00:04:24,386 --> 00:04:26,462
You must have got a dud; I'm sorry.

102
00:04:26,462 --> 00:04:27,474
Let's try again.

103
00:04:27,474 --> 00:04:29,619
[multiple explosions]

104
00:04:29,619 --> 00:04:31,433
Hooray!

105
00:04:31,433 --> 00:04:33,342
Sorry for ruining the surprise.

106
00:04:33,342 --> 00:04:36,241
I know it's never as good
trying to do it again,

107
00:04:36,241 --> 00:04:39,277
but I think we can agree that
the results are what I wanted.

108
00:04:39,277 --> 00:04:43,637
I think surprises where people end up
dead are always the biggest ones.

109
00:04:43,637 --> 00:04:46,133
Oh, man, aren't these guys done already?

110
00:04:46,669 --> 00:04:47,492
Man...

111
00:04:48,058 --> 00:04:50,801
You guys shooting me isn't
helping my aim any.

112
00:04:52,052 --> 00:04:53,479
There we go.

113
00:04:53,479 --> 00:04:54,234
Thanks!

114
00:04:54,708 --> 00:04:55,834
Hello?

115
00:04:57,246 --> 00:04:57,968
Ah!

116
00:05:00,047 --> 00:05:01,434
Yes! That's good!

117
00:05:02,815 --> 00:05:08,586
Yes, run towards my gunshots! That helps
me out a lot. You have no idea.

118
00:05:08,586 --> 00:05:10,467
So, did I miss anyone?

119
00:05:10,467 --> 00:05:12,094
Raise your hand if I didn't--

120
00:05:12,094 --> 00:05:14,059
HECU #1: No sign objective, sir.

121
00:05:14,059 --> 00:05:14,963
HECU #2: Area secure, sir.

122
00:05:14,963 --> 00:05:20,161
Okay, well, I can't tell if you're just a
voice in my head, so you don't count.

123
00:05:20,161 --> 00:05:24,441
So, yeah, I don't see the soldiers
surviving this, even without me.

124
00:05:24,441 --> 00:05:30,045
Like, the theory is that this is a
cover up, which I still think makes no sense.

125
00:05:30,045 --> 00:05:34,469
It's too big. That's like trying to
cover up the President being assassinated.

126
00:05:34,469 --> 00:05:36,497
"Oh, yeah, the President's fine.

127
00:05:36,497 --> 00:05:40,418
"He totally did not get his head
blown apart on national television."

128
00:05:40,418 --> 00:05:44,142
But fine. We're going to 'cover
this up', but the thing is--

129
00:05:44,142 --> 00:05:45,167
Ooh.

130
00:05:46,321 --> 00:05:48,846
Oh, sweet. This is a great idea.

131
00:05:48,846 --> 00:05:51,045
I can see why they built it this way.

132
00:05:51,045 --> 00:05:55,498
I'm not doing anything the warehouse workers
haven't done a hundred times already.

133
00:05:55,498 --> 00:05:56,467
Aww.

134
00:05:57,511 --> 00:05:58,268
[gunshots]

135
00:05:58,268 --> 00:06:01,159
Hey, stop it, Cargo Commando!

136
00:06:01,159 --> 00:06:03,496
[missiles whistling]
I hear something.

137
00:06:03,496 --> 00:06:05,299
[explosions]
Oh!

138
00:06:05,299 --> 00:06:07,841
They just bombed their own
troops again!

139
00:06:07,841 --> 00:06:10,817
This is exactly what
I'm talking about!

140
00:06:10,817 --> 00:06:15,020
Hey, they're bombing! I'm
outside! I didn't even notice!

141
00:06:15,020 --> 00:06:17,345
Jesus, how is it night already?!

142
00:06:17,345 --> 00:06:21,081
Well, that's it. I blacked out.
There's no other explanation.

143
00:06:21,081 --> 00:06:23,865
This is what happens
when I play pharmacist.

144
00:06:23,865 --> 00:06:25,200
Although...

145
00:06:25,747 --> 00:06:28,634
I still feel pretty great!

146
00:06:29,176 --> 00:06:32,171
HECU #3: Squad, quiet down.

147
00:06:32,171 --> 00:06:32,963
HECU #4: Negative.

148
00:06:32,963 --> 00:06:35,922
"Squad, quiet down." "Negative."

149
00:06:35,922 --> 00:06:37,532
All right, works for me.

150
00:06:37,532 --> 00:06:39,500
I'm happy to know where everyone is.

151
00:06:40,678 --> 00:06:42,159
You are there...

152
00:06:42,884 --> 00:06:44,216
Aaah.

153
00:06:44,216 --> 00:06:46,661
Ah, and I am here.

154
00:06:46,661 --> 00:06:50,642
I think that's about the best communication
I'm going to have with the military.

155
00:06:50,642 --> 00:06:52,677
They can't even spell my name right.

156
00:06:52,677 --> 00:06:56,408
But, it's alright. Again, no one
is going to leave here alive.

157
00:06:56,408 --> 00:06:58,167
Especially not the soldiers.

158
00:06:58,777 --> 00:06:59,781
Nyah!

159
00:06:59,781 --> 00:07:01,534
Are these secret documents?

160
00:07:03,478 --> 00:07:04,567
What was I doing?

161
00:07:05,071 --> 00:07:06,946
HECU #5: Okay, check in.

162
00:07:06,946 --> 00:07:08,342
I don't remember.

163
00:07:08,342 --> 00:07:11,871
But yeah, the thing about the
soldiers is that, if this is a cover up,

164
00:07:11,871 --> 00:07:16,461
the government already doesn't trust
its top secret researchers in the country,

165
00:07:16,461 --> 00:07:18,934
so why is it going to trust
its special forces?

166
00:07:20,754 --> 00:07:23,565
See, look at that. I bet they
didn't even identify me.

167
00:07:23,565 --> 00:07:26,272
I bet I could disguise myself in
one of their uniforms

168
00:07:26,272 --> 00:07:28,941
and it wouldn't make a
damned bit of difference.

169
00:07:28,941 --> 00:07:31,868
There has been a LOT of friendly
fire around here.

170
00:07:36,297 --> 00:07:40,235
Okay, that's it. If you can't behave
yourself, you can have time out, mister.

171
00:07:40,235 --> 00:07:41,033
HECU #6: MOVE!

172
00:07:42,580 --> 00:07:43,500
What was that?

173
00:07:45,205 --> 00:07:47,507
Okay, let's keep it that way.

174
00:07:47,507 --> 00:07:52,356
So, besides these soldiers tripping over
themselves to kill each other before I do,

175
00:07:52,356 --> 00:07:54,334
they may have bigger problems.

176
00:07:55,644 --> 00:07:57,862
Because, if they're doing
the cover up job,

177
00:07:57,862 --> 00:08:01,590
somebody else is going to
cover up the cover up job.

178
00:08:01,590 --> 00:08:04,065
Okay, I like what I'm seeing here.

179
00:08:04,065 --> 00:08:07,000
I'M OVER HERE! YOO-HOO!

180
00:08:08,845 --> 00:08:09,500
Perfect.

181
00:08:10,842 --> 00:08:13,801
I love these guys that
run towards me!

182
00:08:14,659 --> 00:08:16,945
They are a dying breed.

183
00:08:16,945 --> 00:08:18,812
Eh, I think that's the last of them.

184
00:08:18,812 --> 00:08:20,793
Come and check out the noise!

185
00:08:20,793 --> 00:08:21,200
Hup!

186
00:08:22,555 --> 00:08:24,167
Was that guy waving at me?

187
00:08:25,665 --> 00:08:28,713
"Yeah, head to the left,
I saw him over there!"

188
00:08:28,713 --> 00:08:31,047
Okay, THAT'S the last of them.

189
00:08:31,047 --> 00:08:31,504
[gunshots]

190
00:08:31,504 --> 00:08:33,050
Ohhhh!

191
00:08:33,050 --> 00:08:34,661
You're pulling THAT shit on me?

192
00:08:34,661 --> 00:08:35,667
HECU #7: LET'S GO!

193
00:08:37,268 --> 00:08:38,534
Umm...

194
00:08:38,534 --> 00:08:40,721
I am so confused.

195
00:08:40,721 --> 00:08:43,599
Did that guy run into his own grenade?

196
00:08:43,599 --> 00:08:46,606
Or did somebody in the shadows
throw one at him?

197
00:08:46,606 --> 00:08:51,728
Or, was he just charging me, suicide-bomber
style, and get his timing wrong?

198
00:08:51,728 --> 00:08:54,937
Is that how we train them?
As suicide-bombers?

199
00:08:54,937 --> 00:08:56,309
So many questions.

200
00:08:56,309 --> 00:09:00,319
Man, something's definitely off
with this cover up operation.

201
00:09:00,319 --> 00:09:01,848
Yeah, nobody's here.

202
00:09:01,848 --> 00:09:05,834
With THIS much friendly fire, I
don't think it's an accident.

203
00:09:05,834 --> 00:09:06,801
What the hell?!

204
00:09:10,702 --> 00:09:12,067
Yeah, I'm still here!

205
00:09:15,856 --> 00:09:19,133
Yep, they just blew up another
guy with their own grenade.

206
00:09:21,938 --> 00:09:23,801
I should turn this light off.

207
00:09:24,827 --> 00:09:29,260
I wish I had a walkie-talkie so I could just
throw that down and transmit my voice

208
00:09:29,260 --> 00:09:32,605
so they would all open fire
blindly and shoot each other.

209
00:09:32,605 --> 00:09:34,626
I mean, we're halfway
there already.

210
00:09:34,626 --> 00:09:36,534
They're not what I would call discriminate.

211
00:09:37,737 --> 00:09:38,050
Yep.

212
00:09:38,463 --> 00:09:38,813
Yep.

213
00:09:39,333 --> 00:09:43,040
All these bodies and gunshots
are trying to ruin my mood.

214
00:09:43,040 --> 00:09:45,184
But it's going to take more than that!

215
00:09:45,184 --> 00:09:48,347
I have the power of chemistry on my side.

216
00:09:48,347 --> 00:09:51,095
Anyway, what the fuck did I just see?

217
00:09:51,095 --> 00:09:54,128
It's like the soldiers were
waiting until I showed up,

218
00:09:54,128 --> 00:09:56,987
then executed the scientist in front of me.

219
00:09:56,987 --> 00:09:59,444
I mean, why bother?
I don't know these people.

220
00:09:59,444 --> 00:10:01,581
I know this was directed at me

221
00:10:01,581 --> 00:10:05,968
because there's no way they didn't hear all
the gunshots and explosions prior to this.

222
00:10:05,968 --> 00:10:09,133
This smells better than I
thought, but still bad.

223
00:10:09,974 --> 00:10:12,916
Okay, I'm coming up with
three possible options

224
00:10:12,916 --> 00:10:15,101
for what's going on here
with the military.

225
00:10:15,101 --> 00:10:16,534
Now, the first option...

226
00:10:18,964 --> 00:10:19,755
Um...

227
00:10:20,507 --> 00:10:22,054
What was I thinking about?

228
00:10:22,054 --> 00:10:23,756
[explosion]
Waah!

229
00:10:23,756 --> 00:10:27,687
Maybe this is a bad time
for me to spacing out.

230
00:10:27,687 --> 00:10:29,389
Is this a closet?

231
00:10:29,389 --> 00:10:30,200
Hello?

232
00:10:31,269 --> 00:10:32,467
Can you let me in?

233
00:10:33,498 --> 00:10:36,301
I tried blowing up your
door but it didn't work.

234
00:10:36,301 --> 00:10:37,839
SCIENTIST: Wait a minute
and I'll let you in.

235
00:10:37,839 --> 00:10:38,918
Who said that?!

236
00:10:38,918 --> 00:10:39,885
Where are you?

237
00:10:41,184 --> 00:10:45,552
Oh, that must be the ghost. He
sounds different than I imagined.

238
00:10:45,552 --> 00:10:50,475
Hey, it's neon green. Do they throw raves
in here? The acoustics would suck.

239
00:10:50,475 --> 00:10:51,834
[Geiger counter ticking]
Oh, it's radioactive.

240
00:10:52,843 --> 00:10:56,293
Well, at least it's "click click"
and not "clickyclickclickclick".

241
00:10:56,293 --> 00:10:59,117
You can still cut that shit out, though.

242
00:10:59,117 --> 00:11:01,236
Oh, that's what I was thinking about.

243
00:11:01,236 --> 00:11:05,619
So, option one is this is the cover up
and the troops are being covered up, too.

244
00:11:05,619 --> 00:11:08,886
Like one out of every five
troops is secretly a merc

245
00:11:08,886 --> 00:11:11,444
and his job is to kill the other troops.

246
00:11:11,444 --> 00:11:14,122
Then they'll bomb the
place to kill the mercs,

247
00:11:14,122 --> 00:11:16,301
then they'll kill the bomber pilot,

248
00:11:16,301 --> 00:11:21,464
and then write this all up as
a... plane accident. Why not?

249
00:11:21,464 --> 00:11:22,032
SCIENTIST: Freeman?

250
00:11:22,032 --> 00:11:22,466
Whoa!

251
00:11:22,466 --> 00:11:27,346
SCIENTIST: You'll want to work quickly.
Tune the transmitter to the USNRC.

252
00:11:27,346 --> 00:11:30,436
SCIENTIST: I repeat, tune to the USNRC.

253
00:11:30,436 --> 00:11:33,312
Okay, ghost. I guess you know what's best.

254
00:11:33,312 --> 00:11:38,992
So option two is, everybody's on
drugs. Combat time is drug time!

255
00:11:38,992 --> 00:11:42,336
Shoot anybody you want.
It's cool. He's high, too.

256
00:11:42,336 --> 00:11:44,336
Get high before you die!

257
00:11:44,336 --> 00:11:45,331
That's my favorite theory.

258
00:11:45,331 --> 00:11:49,647
SCIENTIST: Excellent. I'm sending the
All Clear and the doors should open now.

259
00:11:49,647 --> 00:11:50,913
SCIENTIST: We'll meet you down below.

260
00:11:50,913 --> 00:11:52,767
No, wait! I don't want to die yet!

261
00:11:53,250 --> 00:11:53,968
FUCK!

262
00:11:55,922 --> 00:11:57,000
Down you go!

263
00:11:58,450 --> 00:12:00,467
YEAH, KISS THE FLOOR, ASSHOLE!

264
00:12:01,400 --> 00:12:03,600
That's good! Carry on!

265
00:12:03,600 --> 00:12:06,297
Shit, I don't think I can
trust the ghost anymore.

266
00:12:06,297 --> 00:12:08,418
I hope he stops talking to me.

267
00:12:08,418 --> 00:12:10,358
I wasn't really prepared for that.

268
00:12:10,358 --> 00:12:12,921
A bunch of people bursting in
trying to kill me,

269
00:12:12,921 --> 00:12:15,240
that's something I've always
been preparing for.

270
00:12:15,240 --> 00:12:16,750
Mentally, anyway.

271
00:12:16,750 --> 00:12:18,664
But a ghost mildly harassing me

272
00:12:18,664 --> 00:12:22,312
and giving me bad advice is just
whole other kind of hell.

273
00:12:22,312 --> 00:12:23,726
Especially here.

274
00:12:23,726 --> 00:12:26,710
I don't need another hell inside
my existing hell.

275
00:12:26,710 --> 00:12:29,034
Hell squared is still hell.

276
00:12:29,034 --> 00:12:31,020
What the hell is this?

277
00:12:31,020 --> 00:12:34,298
All right, they're either sealing
me in or they're breaching.

278
00:12:34,298 --> 00:12:37,345
Somebody thinks they're big and
bad because they're a welder,

279
00:12:37,345 --> 00:12:39,567
but I'm not going to take their
shit either way.

280
00:12:40,443 --> 00:12:41,434
BACK AT YOU!

281
00:12:47,325 --> 00:12:50,144
Okay, I think that slowed them down.

282
00:12:50,144 --> 00:12:53,095
Yeah, you'll think twice
before doing that again.

283
00:12:53,095 --> 00:12:55,508
Especially since you're a skull.

284
00:12:55,508 --> 00:12:58,895
So, how do I lift up this
giant concrete slab?

285
00:12:58,895 --> 00:13:00,467
Is there like a switch?

286
00:13:01,842 --> 00:13:03,819
I'm not feeling one.

287
00:13:03,819 --> 00:13:04,934
Uhh...

288
00:13:06,128 --> 00:13:08,133
I can't fit through this hole.

289
00:13:14,842 --> 00:13:16,567
Stupid ghost...

